---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Reliable Clipboard"
  description="Move editable Varve layers, images, SVG, and text with predictable placement and honest recovery when a clipboard format is unavailable."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="clipboard-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Reliable Clipboard
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="available" />
        <h1>Copy should mean more than “something was written.”</h1>
        <p>
          Varve treats clipboard transfer as a document workflow: preserve the
          editable structure, carry the resources that make it look right, and
          tell you when a fallback is only text.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="transfer-card site-card site-card--surface" aria-labelledby="transfer-title">
        <div class="transfer-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">One coherent transfer</p>
          <h2 id="transfer-title">Structure, resources, and placement travel together.</h2>
          <p>
            Copying a frame includes its descendants and the supported image,
            mask, icon, and mockup resources it references. Paste allocates fresh
            identities, adopts layers into a selected frame, and applies a
            defined placement policy: same-document copies preserve their
            world pose unless a frame is explicitly selected, in which case
            the fragment is centered inside it; foreign or image/SVG content
            is centered in the selected frame or visible canvas viewport.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="transfer-flow" aria-label="Clipboard transfer stages">
          <div><span>01</span><strong>Snapshot</strong><small>Selected roots and dependencies</small></div>
          <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="accent"><span>02</span><strong>Transfer</strong><small>Editable Varve format first</small></div>
          <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div><span>03</span><strong>Rebase</strong><small>Fresh IDs, correct target</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">What it handles</p>
        <h2 id="capabilities-title">Useful across the ways designers work.</h2>
        <div class="capability-grid">
          <article><h3>Editable layer fragments</h3><p>Nested groups and frames remain editable instead of becoming a screenshot or a flat export.</p></article>
          <article><h3>External images and SVG</h3><p>Clipboard files and validated SVG pass through Varve's existing import pipeline, including multiple distinct image items.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Wayland-aware desktop paste</h3><p>On Linux desktop, native MIME transfer keeps editable layer paste available when WebKitGTK cannot expose the rich clipboard to the canvas.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Predictable placement</h3><p>Paste uses the selected visible frame or group as an explicit destination; otherwise it centers foreign content in the canvas viewport without changing your zoom or pan.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Native text editing</h3><p>Textareas, fields, IME composition, Unicode, and caret behavior remain owned by the browser when you are typing.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Specialist buffers stay separate</h3><p>Copy Properties, effect stacks, and guides do not unexpectedly overwrite the system object clipboard.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Cut waits for truth</h3><p>If only a names-only text fallback is available, Cut leaves the original layers in place.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Undo stays local</h3><p>Undo restores a Cut or Paste from document history without rereading or rewriting the system clipboard.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside class="honesty" aria-labelledby="honesty-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Honest boundaries</p>
        <h2 id="honesty-title">Portable does not mean proprietary.</h2>
        <p>
          Varve supports its own validated fragment plus common text, SVG, and
          image representations. It does not claim Figma, Illustrator, or
          Office private clipboard formats without a decoder and evidence.
          Browser and packaged-desktop behavior still depends on the host's
          clipboard permissions and MIME support.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/K-Arthur/varve/blob/main/docs/architecture/clipboard-system.md">Read the clipboard architecture →</a>
      </aside>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .clipboard-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 700px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .page-hero p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .transfer-card, .honesty { background: var(--surface-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .transfer-card h2, .capabilities h2, .honesty h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
  .transfer-intro { max-width: 680px; }
  .transfer-intro p:not(.eyebrow), .honesty p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .transfer-flow { align-items: stretch; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: 2rem; }
  .transfer-flow > div:not(.arrow) { border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); }
  .transfer-flow .accent { background: var(--surface-accent-soft); border-color: var(--border-accent); }
  .transfer-flow span { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .7rem; }
  .transfer-flow strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .transfer-flow small { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.4; }
  .arrow { align-self: center; color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .capabilities { padding: 4rem 0; }
  .capability-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .capability-grid article { border-top: 2px solid var(--border-accent); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .capability-grid h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .capability-grid p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
  .honesty a { color: var(--text-link); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .transfer-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .arrow { justify-self: center; transform: rotate(90deg); } .capability-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
